//@version=6
// =============================================================================
//  Riptide LIT Structure - v0.7.15 Window-Cohort Near Calibration
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  Inside bars -> pullbacks -> pivots -> IDM -> BOS -> CHoCH -> trend.
//  v0.7.15: every IDM is rendered as one continuous owned line from pullback
//  start through migration/take. Renderer-only; frozen IDM logic unchanged.
//
//  A separate strategy family. It shares no state, no filters and no
//  assumptions with the Riptide liquidity-sweep engine, and it places no
//  trades: it marks structure and nothing else.
//
//  NO FIXED SWING LENGTHS. No pivot length, no left/right bars, no zigzag
//  percentage, no fractal size. A pivot exists only because a pullback
//  completed.
//
//  NON-REPAINTING. Every level is set from bars that had already closed when
//  it was set. No lookahead, no security(). The only delays are the ones the
//  rules require: a correction breaking out, a body closing, a Hidden Shadow
//  resolving. A level also cannot be broken on the bar that created it, so
//  nothing is decided from an ordering OHLC cannot supply.
//
//  [SRC] marks a rule taken from the reference. [INF] marks a decision made
//  where the reference is silent - those are the first things to change if the
//  chart disagrees with the references.
//
//  ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//  WHAT CHANGED FROM v0.1, AND WHY
//
//  1. THE DEVIATION IS REMOVED. v0.1 moved a correction's confirmation level
//     down each time the correction made a deeper low. That was a patch, and
//     it covered a different bug: v0.1 ran a demand tracker and a supply
//     tracker permanently in parallel feeding one shared pivot stream, so a
//     demand correction opened during a downtrend could never confirm - one
//     stayed open for 9200 bars. The documented algorithm is TREND-RELATIVE.
//     v0.2 orients each detector to its own context's direction and
//     re-initialises it on a flip. The confirmation level is then FIXED at the
//     correction-start candle, exactly as documented, and nothing starves.
//
//  2. NO IDM DURING THE BOS RACE. v0.1 published a new inducement while a BOS
//     was still unresolved. Corrections found in that phase are now cached as
//     LATENT and the latest matching one is activated when the boundary
//     resolves.
//
//  3. NO SAME-BAR CASCADE. Every level records the bar it was created on and
//     cannot be evaluated for a break until the next one, and each context
//     performs at most one major transition per bar.
//
//  4. THE DEPTHS ARE NO LONGER ONE ANALYTICAL CANDLE STREAM. Main, Internal
//     and Deep each own their own persistent-mother normalizer, pullback
//     detector, direction, phase, levels and history. A candle suppressed as
//     an inside bar for Main can still be structurally meaningful to Internal.
//     This is required by the source rule that inside bars are INTERNAL /
//     FRACTAL activity rather than candles that disappear globally.
//
//  MEASURED BEFORE THIS FILE WAS WRITTEN - research/lit_v02.py, 8 symbols,
//  120 days of Min15: zero invariant violations at every depth, zero same-bar
//  ambiguity, 71% of Main BOS locks broke and 27% were abandoned when the
//  CHoCH resolved first, median lock distance 1.43%.
//
//  ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//  THE INFERRED DECISIONS THAT MATTER, IN ORDER OF HOW LIKELY THEY ARE WRONG
//
//  1. HOW THE DEPTHS ARE SEPARATED. Main / Internal / Deep now own separate
//     persistent-mother normalizers. This is not a fixed swing-length trick:
//     every depth still uses the exact same LIT pullback state machine. The
//     distinction is that an inside candle has no value to its PARENT depth
//     but remains raw price that a CHILD depth may organize independently.
//     v0.7 supersedes this earlier inference: child contexts are now reseeded
//     by published parent pullback scopes, not by parent BOS/CHoCH continuation.
//
//  2. THE LEG RESET. [SRC] says the leg start survives IDM migration and that
//     BOS is the leg extreme through the IDM break. It does not say when the
//     leg restarts. Never restarting makes BOS the all-time extreme, which
//     can never break. Here it survives migration - the invariant is checked -
//     and restarts at the CHoCH point on a BOS break and on a flip.
//
//  3. BOOTSTRAP. A context starts UNDEFINED and runs both orientations until
//     one confirms a correction; that sets the direction and the other is
//     discarded. No average, no candle colour, and no bootstrap state
//     survives into mature behaviour.
//
//  4. Exact equality is not a break. Both sides of a mother range taken in one
//     candle closes the group without guessing an order. Body & Sweep keeps
//     its migrated level after a Hidden Shadow rejection.
// =============================================================================
//  v0.7 SCOPED-HIERARCHY PROFILE:
//  - Main remains the primary structure context.
//  - Internal no longer runs globally. A Main pullback START opens the
//    active Internal scope; Internal is reset/reseeded only when that Main
//    pullback scope is replaced (or invalidated by a Main CHoCH flip).
//  - Deep is owned the same way by an Internal pullback START.
//  - Child direction is independently bootstrapped inside its owning scope;
//    it is NOT forced opposite the parent.
//  - No ATR filter, timeout, pivot length, zigzag, Main promotion, or new
//    structural rule is introduced. This is a hierarchy/ownership change only.
//  - Child drawings are gated by their owning scope, so i/ii levels stop at
//    scope boundaries instead of leaking across unrelated structure.
//  - Labels use a controlled centre position + depth-aware vertical clearance.
//
indicator("Riptide LIT Structure — v0.7.9 CAL", "Riptide LIT",
     overlay          = true,
     max_lines_count  = 500,
     max_labels_count = 500,
     max_boxes_count  = 500,
     max_bars_back    = 5000)

// ═══════════════════════════ CONSTANTS ══════════════════════════════════════
int DIR_NONE = 0
int DIR_BULL = 1
int DIR_BEAR = -1

// [SRC] The four documented phases.
int PH_DISCOVER = 0   // trend known, no IDM yet
int PH_TRACK    = 1   // IDM active, may migrate
int PH_SEEK     = 2   // IDM taken, BOS locked, no opposing CHoCH
int PH_LOCK     = 3   // BOS and CHoCH both active - no IDM may exist

int BRK_SHADOW = 0
int BRK_BODY   = 1
int BRK_SWEEP  = 2

int PB_IMPULSE = 1
int PB_ACTIVE  = 2

// Context event codes. In v0.7 these no longer define child ownership.
// Child ownership comes from PUBLISHED parent pullbacks; CHoCH only invalidates
// the old directional child scope.
int EVT_NONE  = 0
int EVT_IDM   = 1
int EVT_BOS   = 2
int EVT_CHOCH = 3

// ═══════════════════════════ 1. INPUTS ══════════════════════════════════════
string gEng = "1. Engine"
string gBrk = "2. Breakout rules"
string gHS  = "3. Hidden Shadow"
string gShow = "4. Structure"
string gPB  = "5. Pullback zones"
string gCol = "6. Appearance"
string gDbg = "7. Panels and debug"

bool cfgConfirm = input.bool(true, "Only update structure on closed bars",
     group = gEng,
     tooltip = "On: a bar is read once it has closed, which is the only way the chart can promise that what you see now is what it would have said then.\n\nOff: levels can move inside a forming bar and settle differently when it closes.")
string devMode = input.string("All depths", "Development mode", group = gEng,
     options = ["All depths", "MAIN ONLY"],
     tooltip = "MAIN ONLY silences Internal and Deep entirely - engine and drawing both. Main has to be right before recursion is worth looking at, and hiding a Main problem behind child levels is how v0.1 got through review.")

// ── 2. Breakout rules ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// [SRC] One engine, four users.
string mPB = input.string("Shadow", "Pullback confirmation", group = gBrk,
     options = ["Shadow", "Body", "Body & Sweep"],
     tooltip = "How a correction proves it is over.\n\nShadow: a wick back through the level.\n\nBody: a close beyond it.\n\nBody & Sweep: a close beyond the SWEEP LEVEL - the furthest a wick pushed through and failed. Once a level is swept, closing beyond the OLD level is no longer enough.")
string mIDM = input.string("Shadow", "IDM break", group = gBrk,
     options = ["Shadow", "Body", "Body & Sweep"],
     tooltip = "Taking inducement IS a wick event - the stops under that low fill whether or not the candle closes there - which is why this defaults to Shadow.")
string mBOS = input.string("Body & Sweep", "BOS break", group = gBrk,
     options = ["Shadow", "Body", "Body & Sweep"])
string mCH = input.string("Body & Sweep", "CHoCH break", group = gBrk,
     options = ["Shadow", "Body", "Body & Sweep"])

bool hsPB = input.bool(false, "Hidden Shadow on pullback", group = gHS,
     tooltip = "No effect while the matching break mode is Shadow: a wick break is already a wick break.")
bool hsIDM = input.bool(false, "Hidden Shadow on IDM", group = gHS)
bool hsBOS = input.bool(true, "Hidden Shadow on BOS", group = gHS)
bool hsCH = input.bool(true, "Hidden Shadow on CHoCH", group = gHS)

// ── 4. Structure ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
bool showMain = input.bool(true, "Main", group = gShow, inline = "d")
bool showInt = input.bool(true, "Internal", group = gShow, inline = "d")
bool showDeep = input.bool(true, "Deep", group = gShow, inline = "d",
     tooltip = "Deep is owned by the active Internal pullback scope in v0.7. Turn off only to simplify visual calibration.")
bool showIDM = input.bool(true, "IDM", group = gShow, inline = "l")
bool showBOS = input.bool(true, "BOS", group = gShow, inline = "l")
bool showCH = input.bool(true, "CHoCH", group = gShow, inline = "l")
bool showSW = input.bool(true, "Strong / Weak labels", group = gShow,
     tooltip = "[SRC] Display semantics derived from the current structure. Nothing in the engine reads them: in a bullish structure the continuation-side high is WEAK and the reversal-side low is STRONG.")
bool showRetired = input.bool(false, "Mark taken inducements with x",
     group = gShow,
     tooltip = "A retired IDM leaves a small cross where it was taken instead of a full labelled line. Old inducements are the main source of clutter and they are not live information.")
bool showInside = input.bool(false, "Tint inside bars", group = gShow,
     tooltip = "Off by default - on a busy chart the tint reads as another signal. The debug panel reports the rate either way.")
int histMain = input.int(8, "History", minval = 1, maxval = 40, group = gShow,
     inline = "h", tooltip = "Retired levels kept per depth. TradingView caps a script at 500 lines and 500 labels; these are what hold this one inside that.")
int histInt = input.int(6, "", minval = 1, maxval = 40, group = gShow,
     inline = "h")
int histDeep = input.int(3, "", minval = 1, maxval = 40, group = gShow,
     inline = "h")

// ── 5. Pullback zones ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
bool pbMainOn = input.bool(true, "Main zones", group = gPB, inline = "p")
bool pbIntOn = input.bool(true, "Internal zones", group = gPB, inline = "p")
bool pbDeepOn = input.bool(true, "Deep zones", group = gPB, inline = "p")
int histPB = input.int(10, "Zones kept per depth", minval = 1, maxval = 30,
     group = gPB)
string pbEdge = input.string("Initial level", "Zone boundary", group = gPB,
     options = ["Initial level", "Final swept level"],
     tooltip = "[SRC] Visual only. It moves the edge of the box and changes nothing about the pivot or the structure state.")
string mainPbRender = input.string("Hide if started in Boundary Lock",
     "Main PB during Boundary Lock", group = gPB,
     options = ["Show all", "Hide if started in Boundary Lock"],
     tooltip = "Visual policy only. The detector and structure engine are unchanged. When hidden, a Main correction that STARTED while Main was already in Boundary Lock is not drawn as a historical pullback zone after confirmation. Internal/Deep zones are unaffected.")
bool markHiddenPb = input.bool(true, "Debug mark hidden Main PB", group = gPB,
     tooltip = "When Debug is on, place a tiny marker where a Main pullback zone was suppressed by the visual Boundary-Lock policy.")

// ── 6. Appearance ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Riptide's palette, from riptide-indicator.pine, so the charts read as one
// product. Strength is graded by DEPTH rather than by colour so the hierarchy
// survives on a white background - v0.1's faint cyan did not.
color cBull = input.color(#26a69a, "Bullish", group = gCol, inline = "c1")
color cBear = input.color(#ef5350, "Bearish", group = gCol, inline = "c1")
color cIDMBull = input.color(#2962ff, "Bullish IDM", group = gCol, inline = "c2")
color cIDMBear = input.color(#ffb300, "Bearish IDM", group = gCol, inline = "c2")
color cHS = input.color(#9c27b0, "Hidden Shadow", group = gCol, inline = "c3")
int fadeMain = input.int(0, "Fade: Main", minval = 0, maxval = 80,
     group = gCol, inline = "f",
     tooltip = "Transparency per depth. Defaults give Internal roughly three quarters of Main's strength and Deep about half, which is the hierarchy the brief asks for and stays legible on TradingView Light.")
int fadeInt = input.int(10, "Internal", minval = 0, maxval = 80, group = gCol,
     inline = "f")
int fadeDeep = input.int(28, "Deep", minval = 0, maxval = 80, group = gCol,
     inline = "f")
string labelSizeMain = input.string("Normal", "Main label size", group = gCol,
     options = ["Tiny", "Small", "Normal"], inline = "ls")
string labelSizeChild = input.string("Small", "Child labels", group = gCol,
     options = ["Tiny", "Small", "Normal"], inline = "ls")
float labelClearAtr = input.float(0.24, "Label clearance × ATR", minval = 0.00,
     maxval = 0.50, step = 0.01, group = gCol,
     tooltip = "Vertical clearance keeps centered BOS/CHoCH/IDM labels from sitting behind candle bodies. Visual only.")

// ── 7. Panels ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
bool showPanel = input.bool(false, "Guidance panel", group = gDbg)
// Developer diagnostics are intentionally not exposed in the normal UI.
// Keep the engine invariant counters internally, but do not cover the chart
// with the old bottom-left debug table.
bool showDbg = false
bool showStats = input.bool(true, "Structure statistics", group = gDbg,
     tooltip = "Compact first-passage statistics for the selected structure depth. These are structure diagnostics, not trade performance.")
string statsDepth = input.string("Main", "Statistics depth", group = gDbg,
     options = ["Main", "Internal", "Deep"])
string statsWindow = input.string("Visible chart", "Statistics window", group = gDbg,
     options = ["Visible chart", "All loaded bars"],
     tooltip = "Visible chart cohorts calibration events whose opportunity begins inside the current viewport. Use the same viewport as the reference indicator when calibrating its table.")
bool showNearScan = input.bool(true, "Near-rule calibration scan", group = gDbg,
     tooltip = "Research only. Counts first entries into several geometric 'near' candidates while BOS and CHoCH are both active. It does not alter structure. Target reference totals on the ZEC 30m fixture are BOS=29 and CHoCH=14.")

// ═══════════════════════════ 2. TYPES ═══════════════════════════════════════
// [SRC] One break engine, four users: pullback, IDM, BOS, CHoCH.
type Brk
    float base = na          // the level as first set - BODY judges this
    float act = na           // BODY_SWEEP migrates this and judges it instead
    int dir = 0
    int mode = 0
    bool useHS = false
    bool pend = false        // a body candidate waiting on Hidden Shadow
    float hsLvl = na
    float hsHi = na
    float hsLo = na
    float hsMomHi = na       // the candidate candle's own range
    float hsMomLo = na
    bool swept = false
    bool shadow = false      // a Hidden Shadow rejection fired this bar
    int sweeps = 0           // length of the current sweep chain
    int lastSweepBar = na
    float lastSweepPx = na

// [SRC] Persistent mother-range normalizer. IMPORTANT: each structure depth
// owns one. Main suppression must not globally delete candles that can form
// Internal/Deep structure.
type Norm
    float hi = na
    float lo = na
    float op = na
    float cl = na
    int hiBar = na
    int loBar = na
    int hiT = na
    int loT = na
    int insideCount = 0
    int bothCount = 0

// [SRC] The documented two-phase correction tracker, ORIENTED to a trend.
type PBDet
    int dir = 1
    int state = 1
    float trkHi = na
    float trkLo = na
    int startBar = na
    int startPhase = na      // phase when THIS correction opened; render/debug metadata only
    bool startedInLock = false
    float conf = na          // FIXED at correction start - never chases price
    float initLvl = na
    float rngHi = na
    int rngHiBar = na
    float rngLo = na
    int rngLoBar = na
    int rngHiT = na
    int rngLoT = na
    Brk b
    bool hit = false         // a correction confirmed on this bar
    float hitPx = na
    int hitBar = na
    int hitT = na
    int hitFrom = na
    int hitFromT = na
    float hitEdge = na

// [§11] createdBar is what stops a level being broken by the bar that made it.
type Lvl
    float px = na
    int bar = na
    int barT = na          // the anchor as a TIMESTAMP - see RE10026 note
    int createdBar = na
    bool on = false
    Brk b

// v0.7: child structure is owned by a confirmed parent pullback scope.
// A scope stays live until a newer published parent pullback replaces it, or
// the parent CHoCH invalidates the old directional scope.
type Scope
    bool active = false
    int id = 0
    int openedBar = na
    int fromT = na
    int confirmT = na
    float hi = na
    float lo = na

type Ctx
    int depth = 0
    int dir = 0
    int phase = 0
    PBDet det
    PBDet boot
    int legBar = na
    float legPx = na
    float legHi = na
    int legHiBar = na
    int legHiT = na
    float legLo = na
    int legLoBar = na
    int legLoT = na
    float phHi = na
    int phHiBar = na
    int phHiT = na
    float phLo = na
    int phLoBar = na
    int phLoT = na
    Lvl idm
    Lvl bos
    Lvl ch
    float latPx = na
    int latBar = na
    int latT = na
    int latFromT = na
    int idmDrawT = na
    bool racing = false
    line lnIdm = na
    label lbIdm = na
    line lnBos = na
    label lbBos = na
    line lnCh = na
    label lbCh = na
    array<line> junkL
    array<label> junkB
    array<box> zones
    array<label> swMarks
    label weakDot = na
    label weakTxt = na
    label strongDot = na
    label strongTxt = na
    line dbgBase = na
    line dbgAct = na
    int nPivot = 0
    int nIdm = 0
    int nIdmBreak = 0
    int nBos = 0
    int nCh = 0
    int nFlip = 0
    int nLatent = 0
    // Reference-table calibration counters. These are presentation/instrumentation
    // only; they never feed the structure engine.
    int statIdmRaceTotal = 0
    int statIdmToBos = 0
    int statIdmToChoch = 0
    bool statRaceArmed = false
    // "Near" second-stage counters are intentionally left unarmed until the
    // exact reference definition is source-confirmed. We do not invent a rule
    // just to force a percentage match.
    int statBosNearTotal = 0
    int statBosNearOppPb = 0
    int statBosNearBreak = 0
    int statChNearTotal = 0
    int statChNearOppPb = 0
    int statChNearBreak = 0
    // v0.7.9 source-shaped near races. A near event is a raw touch/penetration
    // of an active boundary that does NOT confirm that boundary's configured
    // structural break on the same bar. The event then races a valid break
    // against a reach of the latest published pullback range. Instrumentation
    // only: these fields never feed structural state.
    bool statBosNearArmed = false
    bool statChNearArmed = false
    float statBosNearPbTop = na
    float statBosNearPbBot = na
    float statChNearPbTop = na
    float statChNearPbBot = na
    float lastPubPbTop = na
    float lastPubPbBot = na
    // v0.7.15 calibration-only pullback registry. This does NOT feed the
    // LIT state machine. It lets the reference-shaped Near statistic target
    // the nearest published pullback on the OPPOSITE side of the touched
    // structural boundary instead of blindly using the latest PB.
    array<float> statPbTops
    array<float> statPbBots
    // A structural boundary may be approached repeatedly. The reference table
    // appears to count a boundary opportunity once, not re-arm the same level
    // after an Opp-PB excursion. Track the exact level instance by createdBar.
    int statBosNearSeenLevel = na
    int statChNearSeenLevel = na
    // Near-rule calibration scan. These counters are DIAGNOSTIC ONLY. A count
    // is a rising-edge entry into the candidate zone while BOS+CHoCH are both
    // active. No candidate feeds the state machine.
    int calBosTouch = 0
    int calChTouch = 0
    int calBos10 = 0
    int calCh10 = 0
    int calBos20 = 0
    int calCh20 = 0
    int calBos25 = 0
    int calCh25 = 0
    int calBos33 = 0
    int calCh33 = 0
    int calBos50 = 0
    int calCh50 = 0
    int calBosPb = 0
    int calChPb = 0
    bool calBosTouchOn = false
    bool calChTouchOn = false
    bool calBos10On = false
    bool calCh10On = false
    bool calBos20On = false
    bool calCh20On = false
    bool calBos25On = false
    bool calCh25On = false
    bool calBos33On = false
    bool calCh33On = false
    bool calBos50On = false
    bool calCh50On = false
    bool calBosPbOn = false
    bool calChPbOn = false
    float calLastPbHeight = na
    // True only on a bar where the confirmed pullback is actually PUBLISHED
    // into this context as an IDM. Latent corrections formed during SEEK/LOCK
    // remain analytical state but are not rendered as parent pullback zones.
    bool pbPublished = false
    // v0.7.6: child scope begins when the parent correction STARTS, not when it confirms.
    // This lets Internal/Deep observe the bars that actually form inside the parent pullback.
    bool pbStarted = false
    int pbStartDir = 0
    bool markOn = false
    float markPx = na
    int markT = na
    int nBad = 0
    string lastBad = ""
    string lastEvent = "-"

// ═══════════════════════════ 3. BREAK ENGINE ════════════════════════════════
modeOf(string s) =>
    s == "Shadow" ? BRK_SHADOW : s == "Body" ? BRK_BODY : BRK_SWEEP

arm(Brk b, float lvl, int d, int mode, bool useHS) =>
    b.base := lvl
    b.act := lvl
    b.dir := d
    b.mode := mode
    b.useHS := useHS
    b.pend := false
    b.swept := false
    b.shadow := false
    b.sweeps := 0
    b.hsLvl := na

disarm(Brk b) =>
    b.base := na
    b.act := na
    b.pend := false
    b.swept := false
    b.shadow := false

// One bar. True only on the bar the break is CONFIRMED - for a Hidden Shadow
// candidate that is the resolver bar, not the candidate bar.
brkStep(Brk b, float o, float h, float l, float c) =>
    bool done = false
    b.swept := false
    b.shadow := false
    if not na(b.base)
        bool up = b.dir > 0
        if b.pend
            // [SRC] Bars contained by the candidate's own range cannot resolve
            // it. Wait for the first that escapes, then judge a synthetic
            // candle spanning candidate through resolver on its CLOSE.
            if not (h < b.hsMomHi and l > b.hsMomLo)
                b.hsHi := math.max(b.hsHi, h)
                b.hsLo := math.min(b.hsLo, l)
                b.pend := false
                if up ? c > b.hsLvl : c < b.hsLvl
                    done := true
                else
                    // [INF] After a rejection Body & Sweep keeps the level it
                    // had already migrated to rather than resetting to base.
                    b.shadow := true
        else
            bool raw = false
            if b.mode == BRK_SHADOW
                raw := up ? h > b.base : l < b.base
            else if b.mode == BRK_BODY
                raw := up ? c > b.base : c < b.base
            else
                // [SRC] A wick through that closes back inside has SWEPT. The
                // threshold moves to it; the old level is no longer enough.
                if up and h > b.act and c <= b.act
                    b.act := h
                    b.swept := true
                    b.sweeps += 1
                    b.lastSweepBar := bar_index
                    b.lastSweepPx := h
                else if not up and l < b.act and c >= b.act
                    b.act := l
                    b.swept := true
                    b.sweeps += 1
                    b.lastSweepBar := bar_index
                    b.lastSweepPx := l
                raw := up ? c > b.act : c < b.act
            if raw
                if b.useHS and b.mode != BRK_SHADOW
                    b.pend := true
                    b.hsLvl := b.mode == BRK_SWEEP ? b.act : b.base
                    b.hsHi := h
                    b.hsMomHi := h
                    b.hsLo := l
                    b.hsMomLo := l
                else
                    done := true
    done

// ═══════════════════════════ 4. INSIDE BARS ═════════════════════════════════
// [SRC] Persistent mother range. A mother survives all contained candles.
// Crucially, this normalization is PER DEPTH: Main can ignore a candle while
// Internal or Deep still sees it through its own mother lifecycle.
seedNorm(Norm n, float o, float h, float l, float c, int i, int t) =>
    n.hi := h
    n.lo := l
    n.op := o
    n.cl := c
    n.hiBar := i
    n.loBar := i
    n.hiT := t
    n.loT := t

normStep(Norm n, float ro, float rh, float rl, float rc, int i, int t, bool enabled) =>
    bool emit = false
    bool insideNow = false
    bool bothNow = false
    float eo = na
    float eh = na
    float el = na
    float ec = na
    int eHiBar = na
    int eLoBar = na
    int eHiT = na
    int eLoT = na
    if enabled
        if na(n.hi)
            seedNorm(n, ro, rh, rl, rc, i, t)
        else
            bool over = rh > n.hi
            bool under = rl < n.lo
            if not over and not under
                insideNow := true
                n.cl := rc
                n.insideCount += 1
            else
                bothNow := over and under
                if bothNow
                    n.bothCount += 1
                emit := true
                eo := n.op
                eh := n.hi
                el := n.lo
                ec := n.cl
                eHiBar := n.hiBar
                eLoBar := n.loBar
                eHiT := n.hiT
                eLoT := n.loT
                seedNorm(n, ro, rh, rl, rc, i, t)
    [emit, eo, eh, el, ec, eHiBar, eLoBar, eHiT, eLoT, insideNow, bothNow]

var Norm normMain = Norm.new()
var Norm normInt = Norm.new()
var Norm normDeep = Norm.new()

// ═══════════════════════════ 5. PULLBACK DETECTOR ═══════════════════════════
// [SRC] Phase A rides the impulse: while each candle makes a new extreme
// without giving back the other side, both tracking levels move with it.
// Phase B begins the instant the opposite tracking level breaks, and the level
// that confirms the correction is fixed AT THAT CANDLE and does not move
// again. v0.1 moved it; that is the deviation this version removes.
reorient(PBDet d, int dir, float h, float l) =>
    d.dir := dir
    d.state := PB_IMPULSE
    d.trkHi := h
    d.trkLo := l
    d.startBar := na
    d.startPhase := na
    d.startedInLock := false
    d.conf := na
    d.hit := false
    disarm(d.b)

detStep(PBDet d, int i, float o, float h, float l, float c, int hiBar,
     int loBar, int hiT, int loT, int mode, bool useHS, int phase) =>
    d.hit := false
    if na(d.trkHi)
        d.trkHi := h
        d.trkLo := l
    else
        bool bull = d.dir == DIR_BULL
        if d.state == PB_IMPULSE
            bool started = bull ? l < d.trkLo : h > d.trkHi
            if started
                // [SRC] The correction starts here and its confirmation level
                // is this candle's opposite extreme, FIXED from now on.
                d.state := PB_ACTIVE
                d.startBar := i
                d.startPhase := phase
                d.startedInLock := phase == PH_LOCK
                d.conf := bull ? h : l
                d.initLvl := d.conf
                d.rngHi := h
                d.rngHiBar := hiBar
                d.rngHiT := hiT
                d.rngLo := l
                d.rngLoBar := loBar
                d.rngLoT := loT
                d.hitFromT := time
                arm(d.b, d.conf, bull ? 1 : -1, mode, useHS)
            else
                bool cont = bull ? (h > d.trkHi and l >= d.trkLo) :
                     (l < d.trkLo and h <= d.trkHi)
                if cont
                    d.trkHi := h
                    d.trkLo := l
        else
            // [SRC] The RANGE grows, the confirmation level does not. A
            // complex correction stays one correction and emits one pivot.
            if h > d.rngHi
                d.rngHi := h
                d.rngHiBar := hiBar
                d.rngHiT := hiT
            if l < d.rngLo
                d.rngLo := l
                d.rngLoBar := loBar
                d.rngLoT := loT
            if brkStep(d.b, o, h, l, c)
                d.hit := true
                d.hitPx := bull ? d.rngLo : d.rngHi
                d.hitBar := bull ? d.rngLoBar : d.rngHiBar
                d.hitT := bull ? d.rngLoT : d.rngHiT
                d.hitFrom := d.startBar
                d.hitEdge := pbEdge == "Initial level" or na(d.b.act) ?
                     d.initLvl : d.b.act
                d.state := PB_IMPULSE
                d.trkHi := h
                d.trkLo := l
                disarm(d.b)
    d.hit

// ═══════════════════════════ 6. STATE MACHINE ═══════════════════════════════
newCtx(int d) =>
    Ctx.new(depth = d, det = PBDet.new(dir = DIR_BULL, b = Brk.new()),
         boot = PBDet.new(dir = DIR_BEAR, b = Brk.new()),
         idm = Lvl.new(b = Brk.new()), bos = Lvl.new(b = Brk.new()),
         ch = Lvl.new(b = Brk.new()), junkL = array.new<line>(),
         junkB = array.new<label>(), zones = array.new<box>(),
         swMarks = array.new<label>(), statPbTops = array.new<float>(),
         statPbBots = array.new<float>())

openScope(Scope sc, PBDet parentDet, int i, int t) =>
    sc.active := true
    sc.id += 1
    sc.openedBar := i
    sc.fromT := parentDet.hitFromT
    sc.confirmT := t
    sc.hi := parentDet.rngHi
    sc.lo := parentDet.rngLo
    0

closeScope(Scope sc) =>
    sc.active := false
    0

sizeOf(string s) =>
    s == "Tiny" ? size.tiny : s == "Normal" ? size.normal : size.small

setLvl(Lvl v, float px, int bar, int barT, int i, int d, int mode, bool hs) =>
    v.px := px
    v.bar := bar
    v.barT := barT
    v.createdBar := i
    v.on := true
    arm(v.b, px, d, mode, hs)

clearLvl(Lvl v) =>
    v.on := false
    disarm(v.b)

ready(Lvl v, int i) =>
    v.on and i > v.createdBar

retire(Ctx x, line ln, label lb, int cap) =>
    // Freeze historical geometry on the exact retirement/break/migration bar.
    // Previously paint() ran after the state transition, so a retired level
    // could stop one bar short and look like a floating/half line.
    if not na(ln)
        line.set_x2(ln, time)
        if not na(lb)
            int lx1 = line.get_x1(ln)
            int mid = lx1 + int((time - lx1) * 0.50)
            label.set_x(lb, mid)
        array.push(x.junkL, ln)
        if array.size(x.junkL) > cap
            line.delete(array.shift(x.junkL))
    if not na(lb)
        array.push(x.junkB, lb)
        if array.size(x.junkB) > cap
            label.delete(array.shift(x.junkB))
    0

// [SRC/§9] A new directional leg. IDM migration never calls this.
legStart(Ctx x, float px, int bar, float h, float l, int hiBar, int loBar,
     int hiT, int loT) =>
    x.legPx := px
    x.legBar := bar
    x.legHi := h
    x.legHiBar := hiBar
    x.legHiT := hiT
    x.legLo := l
    x.legLoBar := loBar
    x.legLoT := loT

flag(Ctx x, bool ok, string name) =>
    if not ok
        x.nBad += 1
        x.lastBad := name
    0

// Calibration helpers. They never mutate structural levels.
// v0.7.15: Visible-chart statistics are COHORTED by event/race start time.
// A race armed left of the viewport is not allowed to resolve inside the viewport
// and inflate the visible sample. Once armed inside the viewport, it may resolve
// later; this matches first-passage cohort semantics.
inStatsWindow(int t) =>
    statsWindow == "All loaded bars" or
     (t >= chart.left_visible_bar_time and t <= chart.right_visible_bar_time)

nearDist(Lvl v, float h, float l) =>
    v.b.dir == 1 ? math.max(v.px - h, 0.0) : math.max(l - v.px, 0.0)

nearTouch(Lvl v, float h, float l) =>
    v.b.dir == 1 ? h >= v.px : l <= v.px

// v0.7.15: choose the nearest previously-published pullback in the direction
// AWAY from the structural boundary that was approached.
// Upper boundary (break dir +1) -> choose nearest PB below it.
// Lower boundary (break dir -1) -> choose nearest PB above it.
// Calibration only; never mutates structure.
pickOppPb(Ctx x, Lvl v) =>
    float outTop = na
    float outBot = na
    float best = na
    int n = array.size(x.statPbTops)
    if n > 0
        for j = 0 to n - 1
            float pt = array.get(x.statPbTops, j)
            float pb = array.get(x.statPbBots, j)
            bool eligible = v.b.dir == 1 ? pt < v.px : pb > v.px
            if eligible
                float d = v.b.dir == 1 ? v.px - pt : pb - v.px
                if na(best) or d < best
                    best := d
                    outTop := pt
                    outBot := pb
    [outTop, outBot]

// Research-only scan of possible meanings of the reference word "near".
// Each candidate counts a NEW ENTRY into its zone, not every bar spent there.
nearScan(Ctx x, int t, float h, float l) =>
    bool live = x.phase == PH_LOCK and x.bos.on and x.ch.on
    if not live
        x.calBosTouchOn := false
        x.calChTouchOn := false
        x.calBos10On := false
        x.calCh10On := false
        x.calBos20On := false
        x.calCh20On := false
        x.calBos25On := false
        x.calCh25On := false
        x.calBos33On := false
        x.calCh33On := false
        x.calBos50On := false
        x.calCh50On := false
        x.calBosPbOn := false
        x.calChPbOn := false
    else
        float span = math.abs(x.bos.px - x.ch.px)
        float db = nearDist(x.bos, h, l)
        float dc = nearDist(x.ch, h, l)
        bool bTouch = nearTouch(x.bos, h, l)
        bool cTouch = nearTouch(x.ch, h, l)
        bool b10 = span > 0 and db <= span * 0.10
        bool c10 = span > 0 and dc <= span * 0.10
        bool b20 = span > 0 and db <= span * 0.20
        bool c20 = span > 0 and dc <= span * 0.20
        bool b25 = span > 0 and db <= span * 0.25
        bool c25 = span > 0 and dc <= span * 0.25
        bool b33 = span > 0 and db <= span / 3.0
        bool c33 = span > 0 and dc <= span / 3.0
        bool b50 = span > 0 and db <= span * 0.50
        bool c50 = span > 0 and dc <= span * 0.50
        bool bPb = not na(x.calLastPbHeight) and x.calLastPbHeight > 0 and db <= x.calLastPbHeight
        bool cPb = not na(x.calLastPbHeight) and x.calLastPbHeight > 0 and dc <= x.calLastPbHeight
        bool count = inStatsWindow(t)
        if bTouch and not x.calBosTouchOn and count
            x.calBosTouch += 1
        if cTouch and not x.calChTouchOn and count
            x.calChTouch += 1
        if b10 and not x.calBos10On and count
            x.calBos10 += 1
        if c10 and not x.calCh10On and count
            x.calCh10 += 1
        if b20 and not x.calBos20On and count
            x.calBos20 += 1
        if c20 and not x.calCh20On and count
            x.calCh20 += 1
        if b25 and not x.calBos25On and count
            x.calBos25 += 1
        if c25 and not x.calCh25On and count
            x.calCh25 += 1
        if b33 and not x.calBos33On and count
            x.calBos33 += 1
        if c33 and not x.calCh33On and count
            x.calCh33 += 1
        if b50 and not x.calBos50On and count
            x.calBos50 += 1
        if c50 and not x.calCh50On and count
            x.calCh50 += 1
        if bPb and not x.calBosPbOn and count
            x.calBosPb += 1
        if cPb and not x.calChPbOn and count
            x.calChPb += 1
        x.calBosTouchOn := bTouch
        x.calChTouchOn := cTouch
        x.calBos10On := b10
        x.calCh10On := c10
        x.calBos20On := b20
        x.calCh20On := c20
        x.calBos25On := b25
        x.calCh25On := c25
        x.calBos33On := b33
        x.calCh33On := c33
        x.calBos50On := b50
        x.calCh50On := c50
        x.calBosPbOn := bPb
        x.calChPbOn := cPb
    0

// [§12] One bar, one context, deterministic order, at most one major
// transition. The returned event still describes this context's structure, but
// v0.7 child ownership is driven by published parent pullback scopes.
ctxStep(Ctx x, bool resetMe, int seedDir, int i, float o, float h, float l, float c,
     int hiBar, int loBar, int hiT, int loT, int cap) =>
    if resetMe
        // v0.7.15 scoped reset. A child is born when the parent correction starts,
        // but its STRUCTURAL DIRECTION is not inherited from the parent.
        // The child must bootstrap its own LIT direction from the candles inside
        // its owning pullback scope. This is critical for iBOS vs iCHoCH identity.
        x.dir := seedDir
        x.phase := PH_DISCOVER
        clearLvl(x.idm)
        clearLvl(x.bos)
        clearLvl(x.ch)
        x.racing := false
        x.statBosNearArmed := false
        x.statChNearArmed := false
        x.statBosNearPbTop := na
        x.statBosNearPbBot := na
        x.statChNearPbTop := na
        x.statChNearPbBot := na
        x.lastPubPbTop := na
        x.lastPubPbBot := na
        x.latPx := na
        x.latFromT := na
        x.idmDrawT := na
        if seedDir == DIR_NONE
            reorient(x.det, DIR_BULL, h, l)
            reorient(x.boot, DIR_BEAR, h, l)
        else
            reorient(x.det, seedDir, h, l)
            reorient(x.boot, -seedDir, h, l)
            legStart(x, seedDir == DIR_BULL ? l : h, i, h, l, hiBar, loBar, hiT, loT)
        retire(x, x.lnIdm, x.lbIdm, cap)
        retire(x, x.lnBos, x.lbBos, cap)
        retire(x, x.lnCh, x.lbCh, cap)
        x.lnIdm := na
        x.lbIdm := na
        x.lnBos := na
        x.lbBos := na
        x.lnCh := na
        x.lbCh := na

    x.markOn := false
    x.pbPublished := false
    x.pbStarted := false
    x.pbStartDir := DIR_NONE
    int pbMode = modeOf(mPB)
    bool hit = false
    if x.dir == DIR_NONE
        // [INFERRED INITIALIZATION] Both orientations run until one confirms a
        // correction. That sets the direction; the other is discarded. No
        // average, no candle colour, and no bootstrap state survives.
        bool up = detStep(x.det, i, o, h, l, c, hiBar, loBar, hiT, loT, pbMode, hsPB, x.phase)
        bool dn = detStep(x.boot, i, o, h, l, c, hiBar, loBar, hiT, loT, pbMode, hsPB, x.phase)
        if up
            x.dir := DIR_BULL
            hit := true
            legStart(x, x.det.hitPx, x.det.hitBar, h, l, hiBar, loBar, hiT, loT)
        else if dn
            x.dir := DIR_BEAR
            hit := true
            x.det.hitPx := x.boot.hitPx
            x.det.hitBar := x.boot.hitBar
            x.det.hitT := x.boot.hitT
            x.det.hitFromT := x.boot.hitFromT
            x.det.hitFrom := x.boot.hitFrom
            x.det.hitEdge := x.boot.hitEdge
            legStart(x, x.boot.hitPx, x.boot.hitBar, h, l, hiBar, loBar, hiT, loT)
        if x.dir != DIR_NONE
            reorient(x.det, x.dir, h, l)
            reorient(x.boot, -x.dir, h, l)
            x.lastEvent := "bootstrap"
    else
        int detStateBefore = x.det.state
        hit := detStep(x.det, i, o, h, l, c, hiBar, loBar, hiT, loT, pbMode, hsPB, x.phase)
        if detStateBefore == PB_IMPULSE and x.det.state == PB_ACTIVE
            x.pbStarted := true
            x.pbStartDir := x.dir

    // running extremes: the leg feeds the BOS lock, the phase feeds the CHoCH
    if na(x.legHi) or h > x.legHi
        x.legHi := h
        x.legHiBar := hiBar
        x.legHiT := hiT
    if na(x.legLo) or l < x.legLo
        x.legLo := l
        x.legLoBar := loBar
        x.legLoT := loT
    if x.phase == PH_SEEK or x.phase == PH_LOCK
        if na(x.phHi) or h > x.phHi
            x.phHi := h
            x.phHiBar := hiBar
            x.phHiT := hiT
        if na(x.phLo) or l < x.phLo
            x.phLo := l
            x.phLoBar := loBar
            x.phLoT := loT

    // Diagnostic only: scan candidate meanings of "near" before any major
    // transition on this bar can replace/clear the active structural levels.
    nearScan(x, time, h, l)

    // [SRC/§8] A confirmed correction is PUBLISHED as an IDM only in the two
    // phases that may hold one. During the BOS race it is cached as LATENT.
    if hit
        x.nPivot += 1
        x.latPx := x.det.hitPx
        x.latBar := x.det.hitBar
        x.latT := x.det.hitT
        x.latFromT := x.det.hitFromT
        if x.phase == PH_DISCOVER or x.phase == PH_TRACK
            // Only this branch publishes the confirmed PB as an active IDM.
            // This is also the only branch that should render an External/
            // Internal/Deep pullback zone. A correction confirmed during
            // SEEK/LOCK is LATENT, not a displayed parent pullback.
            x.pbPublished := true
            x.calLastPbHeight := math.abs(x.det.hitEdge - x.det.hitPx)
            // Preserve the full latest published pullback range for the
            // reference "Opp PB reach" first-passage statistic. This is
            // analytical instrumentation only; IDM/pivot selection is unchanged.
            x.lastPubPbTop := math.max(x.det.hitEdge, x.det.hitPx)
            x.lastPubPbBot := math.min(x.det.hitEdge, x.det.hitPx)
            // Keep a short analytical registry of published PB geometry for
            // Near-stat calibration. This is deliberately independent of the
            // drawing-history cap and does not alter IDM migration.
            array.push(x.statPbTops, x.lastPubPbTop)
            array.push(x.statPbBots, x.lastPubPbBot)
            if array.size(x.statPbTops) > 32
                array.shift(x.statPbTops)
                array.shift(x.statPbBots)
            int legWas = x.legBar
            if x.idm.on
                retire(x, x.lnIdm, x.lbIdm, cap)
                x.lnIdm := na
                x.lbIdm := na
            setLvl(x.idm, x.det.hitPx, x.det.hitBar, x.det.hitT, i,
                 x.dir == DIR_BULL ? -1 : 1, modeOf(mIDM), hsIDM)
            // Rendering starts at the pullback left edge. While active it extends
            // continuously to the current bar; on migration/take retire() freezes
            // the other endpoint on the exact event bar, producing an edge-to-event
            // IDM segment instead of a floating/half historical dash. The structural
            // price remains the pivot (x.idm.barT/x.idm.px).
            // v0.7.15 visual ownership:
            // ONE line owns the entire IDM lifetime. It begins at the pullback
            // correction start and extends continuously until migration/take.
            // No separate bridge, no floating half-segment.
            // Analytical IDM state itself is unchanged.
            x.idmDrawT := x.det.hitFromT
            x.phase := PH_TRACK
            x.nIdm += 1
            x.lastEvent := "IDM"
            flag(x, x.legBar == legWas, "I7 leg moved with IDM")
        else
            x.lastEvent := "latent cached"
            flag(x, not x.idm.on, "I6 IDM live during BOS race")

    bool moved = false
    int outEvent = EVT_NONE

    // [SRC] IDM break. Taking inducement never flips the trend.
    if ready(x.idm, i) and brkStep(x.idm.b, o, h, l, c)
        int was = x.dir
        x.markOn := true
        x.markPx := x.idm.px
        x.markT := time
        clearLvl(x.idm)
        x.idmDrawT := na
        retire(x, x.lnIdm, x.lbIdm, cap)
        x.lnIdm := na
        x.lbIdm := na
        if x.bos.on
            retire(x, x.lnBos, x.lbBos, cap)
            x.lnBos := na
            x.lbBos := na
        setLvl(x.bos, x.dir == DIR_BULL ? x.legHi : x.legLo,
             x.dir == DIR_BULL ? x.legHiBar : x.legLoBar,
             x.dir == DIR_BULL ? x.legHiT : x.legLoT, i,
             x.dir == DIR_BULL ? 1 : -1, modeOf(mBOS), hsBOS)
        x.phHi := h
        x.phHiBar := hiBar
        x.phHiT := hiT
        x.phLo := l
        x.phLoBar := loBar
        x.phLoT := loT
        x.phase := x.ch.on ? PH_LOCK : PH_SEEK
        x.racing := x.ch.on
        // Reference calibration: after IDM is taken, arm a FIRST-TOUCH race
        // between the active BOS and CHoCH levels. Do NOT count the race yet;
        // Total is the number of races that actually resolve by a unique first touch.
        x.statRaceArmed := x.phase == PH_LOCK and inStatsWindow(time)
        x.nIdmBreak += 1
        x.lastEvent := x.phase == PH_LOCK ? "IDM taken - lock" : "IDM taken"
        moved := true
        outEvent := EVT_IDM
        flag(x, x.dir == was, "I2 IDM break flipped direction")

    // Reference-stat first passage uses TOUCH, not confirmed breakout.
    // This is instrumentation only and never mutates structural levels.
    if x.statRaceArmed and not moved
        bool bosTouch = ready(x.bos, i) and (x.bos.b.dir == 1 ? h >= x.bos.px : l <= x.bos.px)
        bool chTouch  = ready(x.ch,  i) and (x.ch.b.dir  == 1 ? h >= x.ch.px  : l <= x.ch.px)
        if bosTouch != chTouch
            if inStatsWindow(time)
                x.statIdmRaceTotal += 1
                x.statIdmToBos += bosTouch ? 1 : 0
                x.statIdmToChoch += chTouch ? 1 : 0
            x.statRaceArmed := false
        else if bosTouch and chTouch
            // Intrabar order is unknowable from OHLC. Exclude ambiguous same-bar ties
            // from the calibration population rather than inventing a path.
            x.statRaceArmed := false

    // v0.7.9 REFERENCE-SHAPED NEAR STATISTICS (instrumentation only).
    // Source v1 definition: "near" = raw touch/penetration of an active
    // structural boundary while that boundary has NOT yet produced a confirmed
    // break. The subsequent first passage is measured against the exact
    // structural break events below (including Hidden Shadow resolution), not
    // against a guessed close rule. The opposite-PB target is snapshotted when
    // the near event arms so later IDM migration cannot move the goalposts.
    bool bosArmedThisBar = false
    bool chArmedThisBar = false
    bool bosPbSeenNow = false
    bool chPbSeenNow = false
    if x.phase == PH_LOCK and x.bos.on and x.ch.on
        bool bosRawTouch = nearTouch(x.bos, h, l)
        bool chRawTouch = nearTouch(x.ch, h, l)
        bool havePb = not na(x.lastPubPbTop) and not na(x.lastPubPbBot)

        if x.statBosNearArmed
            bosPbSeenNow := h >= x.statBosNearPbBot and l <= x.statBosNearPbTop
        if x.statChNearArmed
            chPbSeenNow := h >= x.statChNearPbBot and l <= x.statChNearPbTop

        // A raw touch may be a wick sweep, a Body/Body&Sweep candidate awaiting
        // Hidden Shadow, or simply a failed break. In all three cases the
        // structural engine has not confirmed a break yet at this point.
        // v0.7.15 factorial arm:
        // KEEP the nearest-opposite-PB target from v0.7.11, but REMOVE the
        // one-opportunity-per-level restriction. The reference totals (29/14)
        // are larger than the number produced by the one-shot arm (20/13),
        // so the same still-live structural boundary must be allowed to create
        // a later independent Near race after the prior race has resolved.
        // This is statistics instrumentation only; structural levels and IDM
        // migration are unchanged.
        if not x.statBosNearArmed and bosRawTouch and havePb and inStatsWindow(time)
            [oppTop, oppBot] = pickOppPb(x, x.bos)
            if not na(oppTop) and not na(oppBot)
                x.statBosNearArmed := true
                x.statBosNearPbTop := oppTop
                x.statBosNearPbBot := oppBot
                bosArmedThisBar := true

        if not x.statChNearArmed and chRawTouch and havePb and inStatsWindow(time)
            [oppTopCh, oppBotCh] = pickOppPb(x, x.ch)
            if not na(oppTopCh) and not na(oppBotCh)
                x.statChNearArmed := true
                x.statChNearPbTop := oppTopCh
                x.statChNearPbBot := oppBotCh
                chArmedThisBar := true

    // [SRC] BOS break - continuation. Never flips the trend.
    if not moved and ready(x.bos, i) and brkStep(x.bos.b, o, h, l, c)
        // Exact confirmed BOS event resolves an armed BOS-near race. If the
        // snapshotted opposite PB was also reached on this OHLC bar, order is
        // unknowable and the race is excluded.
        if x.statBosNearArmed
            if not bosPbSeenNow and not bosArmedThisBar
                x.statBosNearTotal += 1
                x.statBosNearBreak += 1
            x.statBosNearArmed := false
        // A BOS continuation invalidates a pending CHoCH-near calibration race.
        x.statChNearArmed := false
        int was = x.dir
        clearLvl(x.bos)
        retire(x, x.lnBos, x.lbBos, cap)
        x.lnBos := na
        x.lbBos := na
        if x.ch.on
            retire(x, x.lnCh, x.lbCh, cap)
            x.lnCh := na
            x.lbCh := na
        float newCh = x.dir == DIR_BULL ? x.phLo : x.phHi
        int newChBar = x.dir == DIR_BULL ? x.phLoBar : x.phHiBar
        int newChT = x.dir == DIR_BULL ? x.phLoT : x.phHiT
        setLvl(x.ch, newCh, newChBar, newChT, i, x.dir == DIR_BULL ? -1 : 1,
             modeOf(mCH), hsCH)
        // [INF] That CHoCH point is where the next leg is measured from.
        legStart(x, newCh, newChBar, h, l, hiBar, loBar, hiT, loT)
        x.phase := PH_DISCOVER
        x.nBos += 1
        x.nCh += 1
        x.lastEvent := "BOS broken"
        moved := true
        outEvent := EVT_BOS
        flag(x, x.dir == was, "I3 BOS break flipped direction")
        // [SRC] Reuse a correction that already formed during the race.
        if not na(x.latPx) and x.latBar > newChBar
            setLvl(x.idm, x.latPx, x.latBar, x.latT, i,
                 x.dir == DIR_BULL ? -1 : 1, modeOf(mIDM), hsIDM)
            x.idmDrawT := x.latFromT
            x.phase := PH_TRACK
            x.nLatent += 1
            x.nIdm += 1

    // [SRC] CHoCH break - the only event allowed to flip. INVARIANT 1.
    if not moved and ready(x.ch, i) and brkStep(x.ch.b, o, h, l, c)
        // Exact confirmed CHoCH event resolves an armed CHoCH-near race.
        if x.statChNearArmed
            if not chPbSeenNow and not chArmedThisBar
                x.statChNearTotal += 1
                x.statChNearBreak += 1
            x.statChNearArmed := false
        // A trend flip invalidates the opposite BOS-near calibration race.
        x.statBosNearArmed := false
        int was = x.dir
        float oldBos = x.bos.on ? x.bos.px :
             (was == DIR_BULL ? x.legHi : x.legLo)
        int oldBar = x.bos.on ? x.bos.bar :
             (was == DIR_BULL ? x.legHiBar : x.legLoBar)
        int oldT = x.bos.on ? x.bos.barT :
             (was == DIR_BULL ? x.legHiT : x.legLoT)
        clearLvl(x.ch)
        retire(x, x.lnCh, x.lbCh, cap)
        x.lnCh := na
        x.lbCh := na
        if x.bos.on
            // The old BOS is retyped as the new CHoCH on a trend flip.
            // Do NOT preserve the old BOS drawing at the same price, otherwise
            // historical BOS + live CHoCH render on top of each other as one line.
            clearLvl(x.bos)
            if not na(x.lnBos)
                line.delete(x.lnBos)
            if not na(x.lbBos)
                label.delete(x.lbBos)
            x.lnBos := na
            x.lbBos := na
        if x.idm.on
            clearLvl(x.idm)
            x.idmDrawT := na
            retire(x, x.lnIdm, x.lbIdm, cap)
            x.lnIdm := na
            x.lbIdm := na
        x.dir := -was
        // [SRC] The old BOS is not discarded - it is retyped as the CHoCH
        // that would flip the new trend back.
        setLvl(x.ch, oldBos, oldBar, oldT, i, was == DIR_BULL ? 1 : -1,
         modeOf(mCH), hsCH)
        legStart(x, oldBos, oldBar, h, l, hiBar, loBar, hiT, loT)
        reorient(x.det, x.dir, h, l)
        x.latPx := na
        x.phase := PH_DISCOVER
        x.racing := false
        x.nFlip += 1
        x.lastEvent := "CHoCH broken - flip"
        moved := true
        outEvent := EVT_CHOCH
        flag(x, x.dir != was, "I1 CHoCH break did not flip")

    // If no structural boundary resolved this bar, reaching the snapshotted
    // latest pullback wins the near race. Do not score a same-bar arm+target;
    // OHLC cannot establish which occurred first.
    if not moved
        if x.statBosNearArmed and bosPbSeenNow and not bosArmedThisBar
            x.statBosNearTotal += 1
            x.statBosNearOppPb += 1
            x.statBosNearArmed := false
        if x.statChNearArmed and chPbSeenNow and not chArmedThisBar
            x.statChNearTotal += 1
            x.statChNearOppPb += 1
            x.statChNearArmed := false

    // INVARIANTS 5 and 11, checked every bar rather than assumed.
    if x.phase == PH_LOCK
        flag(x, x.bos.on and x.ch.on and not x.idm.on, "I5 lock shape wrong")
    if x.bos.on and x.ch.on
        flag(x, x.dir == DIR_BULL ? x.bos.px > x.ch.px : x.bos.px < x.ch.px,
             "I11 BOS/CHoCH sides crossed")
    outEvent

// ═══════════════════════════ 7. RENDER ══════════════════════════════════════
// [§33] Presentation only. Nothing here infers a pivot, a level or a
// direction - it draws what the engine already decided.
float atr = ta.atr(50)

// [§24] One object per active level, updated rather than recreated.
// [§23] The label sits at 70% along the live segment, not at bar_index, so
// active labels do not pile up vertically on the current candle.
// RE10026: a bar-index coordinate has to sit within max_bars_back of the
// current bar, and a structural anchor routinely does not. Timestamps carry no
// such limit, so every drawing here is anchored in bar_time. This is the whole
// fix for the 30m error - the anchors there simply sat further back in bars.
drawLvl(line cur, int x1t, float y, color col, int w, string st) =>
    line out = cur
    if na(out)
        out := line.new(x1t, y, time, y, xloc = xloc.bar_time, color = col,
             style = st, width = w)
    else
        line.set_xy1(out, x1t, y)
        line.set_xy2(out, time, y)
    out

tagLvl(label cur, int x1t, float y, string txt, color col, string sz,
     bool above, float clearance) =>
    label out = cur
    // Keep labels centered on their own live segment, but clear candle bodies.
    // Child levels use slightly less clearance so nesting stays compact.
    int xx = x1t + int((time - x1t) * 0.50)
    float yy = y + (above ? atr * clearance : -atr * clearance)
    if na(out)
        out := label.new(xx, yy, txt, xloc = xloc.bar_time,
             yloc = yloc.price, style = label.style_none, color = na,
             textcolor = col, size = sz)
    else
        label.set_xy(out, xx, yy)
        label.set_text(out, txt)
        label.set_textcolor(out, col)
    out

// [§22] Depth grades by width and transparency, not by washing the colour out.
paint(Ctx x, bool on, string pre, int w, int fade, string sz) =>
    if on and x.dir != DIR_NONE
        color bu = color.new(cBull, fade)
        color be = color.new(cBear, fade)
        bool bull = x.dir == DIR_BULL
        color id = color.new(bull ? cIDMBull : cIDMBear, fade)
        int idmX = not na(x.idmDrawT) ? x.idmDrawT : x.idm.barT
        string idmStyle = x.depth == 0 ? line.style_solid : line.style_dotted
        string bosStyle = x.depth == 0 ? line.style_solid : line.style_dashed
        string chStyle = x.depth == 0 ? line.style_solid : line.style_dashed
        if x.idm.on and showIDM
            // The IDM PRICE is the pivot emitted by the completed pullback.
            // Visual geometry starts at the pullback's left edge, matching the
            // reference while keeping the analytical level anchored to the pivot.
            x.lnIdm := drawLvl(x.lnIdm, idmX, x.idm.px, id, 1, idmStyle)
            x.lbIdm := tagLvl(x.lbIdm, idmX, x.idm.px, pre + "IDM", id,
                 sz, not bull, x.depth == 0 ? labelClearAtr : labelClearAtr * 0.78)
        if x.bos.on and showBOS
            color col = bull ? bu : be
            x.lnBos := drawLvl(x.lnBos, x.bos.barT, x.bos.px, col, 1, bosStyle)
            x.lbBos := tagLvl(x.lbBos, x.bos.barT, x.bos.px, pre + "BOS", col,
                 sz, bull, x.depth == 0 ? labelClearAtr : labelClearAtr * 0.78)
        if x.ch.on and showCH
            color col = bull ? be : bu
            x.lnCh := drawLvl(x.lnCh, x.ch.barT, x.ch.px, col, 1, chStyle)
            x.lbCh := tagLvl(x.lbCh, x.ch.barT, x.ch.px, pre + "CHoCH", col,
                 sz, not bull, x.depth == 0 ? labelClearAtr : labelClearAtr * 0.78)
    0

// [§19] A taken inducement leaves a cross where it was taken. Old inducements
// are the main source of clutter on the reference chart and they are not live
// information, so they get a mark and not a labelled line.
markTaken(Ctx x, bool on, int fade, int cap) =>
    if on and x.markOn and showRetired
        label m = label.new(x.markT, x.markPx, "x", xloc = xloc.bar_time,
             yloc = yloc.price, style = label.style_none, color = na,
             textcolor = color.new(x.dir == DIR_BULL ? cIDMBull : cIDMBear, fade), size = size.tiny)
        array.push(x.junkB, m)
        if array.size(x.junkB) > cap
            label.delete(array.shift(x.junkB))
    0

// [§20] Zones nest: Main large and visible, Internal subordinate, Deep faint.
zone(Ctx x, bool on, int fade, int border) =>
    // Render only confirmed pullbacks that were actually published into the
    // context as IDM. This prevents latent corrections formed while BOS/CHoCH
    // are racing from becoming giant historical boxes over valid child structure.
    if on and x.det.hit and x.pbPublished and not na(x.det.hitFrom)
        bool hideMainLock = x.depth == 0 and
             mainPbRender == "Hide if started in Boundary Lock" and
             x.det.startedInLock
        bool bull = x.det.dir == DIR_BULL
        color col = bull ? cBull : cBear
        float top = bull ? x.det.hitEdge : x.det.hitPx
        float bot = bull ? x.det.hitPx : x.det.hitEdge
        if not hideMainLock
            // [VISUAL POLICY] left = correction START, right = CONFIRMATION.
            // The analytical PB still exists regardless of whether this box is
            // shown. This function never mutates detector/context state.
            int bw = x.depth == 0 ? 1 : 0
            box b = box.new(x.det.hitFromT, top, time, bot, xloc = xloc.bar_time,
                 border_color = color.new(col, border), border_width = bw,
                 bgcolor = color.new(col, fade))
            array.push(x.zones, b)
            if array.size(x.zones) > histPB
                box.delete(array.shift(x.zones))


        else if showDbg and markHiddenPb
            label m = label.new(time, x.det.hitPx, "PB hidden · lock",
                 xloc = xloc.bar_time, yloc = yloc.price, style = label.style_none,
                 color = na, textcolor = color.new(col, 35), size = size.tiny)
            array.push(x.junkB, m)
            if array.size(x.junkB) > histMain
                label.delete(array.shift(x.junkB))
    0

// [DEBUG ONLY] The Body & Sweep threshold made visible: a faint dashed BASE,
// a stronger dotted ACTIVE, and an S-mark at each wick that moved it. This
// exists so the migration can be compared against the reference by eye rather
// than argued about. On measured data the drift is small - the pathological
// ZEC CHoCH moved 0.6% across two sweeps - so expect the two lines to sit
// almost on top of each other. A visible gap is the interesting case.
markSweep(Ctx x, Lvl v) =>
    if v.on and v.b.swept
        label mk = label.new(time, v.b.lastSweepPx,
             "S" + str.tostring(v.b.sweeps), xloc = xloc.bar_time,
             yloc = yloc.price, style = label.style_none, color = na,
             textcolor = color.new(cHS, 20), size = size.tiny)
        array.push(x.swMarks, mk)
        if array.size(x.swMarks) > 40
            label.delete(array.shift(x.swMarks))
    0

sweepDebug(Ctx x, bool on) =>
    if on and showDbg
        markSweep(x, x.bos)
        markSweep(x, x.ch)
    0

drawThreshold(Ctx x) =>
    if showDbg and x.ch.on
        if na(x.dbgBase)
            x.dbgBase := line.new(x.ch.barT, x.ch.px, time, x.ch.px,
                 xloc = xloc.bar_time, color = color.new(#787b86, 40),
                 style = line.style_dashed)
        if na(x.dbgAct)
            x.dbgAct := line.new(x.ch.barT, x.ch.b.act, time, x.ch.b.act,
                 xloc = xloc.bar_time, color = color.new(cHS, 25),
                 style = line.style_dotted, width = 2)
        line.set_xy1(x.dbgBase, x.ch.barT, x.ch.px)
        line.set_xy2(x.dbgBase, time, x.ch.px)
        line.set_xy1(x.dbgAct, x.ch.barT, x.ch.b.act)
        line.set_xy2(x.dbgAct, time, x.ch.b.act)
    0

// ═══════════════════════════ 8. RUN ═════════════════════════════════════════
var Ctx mainC = newCtx(0)
var Ctx intC = newCtx(1)
var Ctx deepC = newCtx(2)

bool mainOnly = devMode == "MAIN ONLY"
bool runInt = showInt and not mainOnly
bool runDeep = runInt and showDeep
bool engineOk = cfgConfirm ? barstate.isconfirmed : true

var Scope intScope = Scope.new()
var Scope deepScope = Scope.new()

// Main normalizes the whole raw chart. Children normalize RAW candles only
// while their parent pullback scope owns them. They are not global engines.
[mOn, mO, mH, mL, mC, mHiBar, mLoBar, mHiT, mLoT, mInside, mBoth] = normStep(normMain, open, high, low, close, bar_index, time, engineOk)
[iOn, iO, iH, iL, iC, iHiBar, iLoBar, iHiT, iLoT, iInside, iBoth] = normStep(normInt, open, high, low, close, bar_index, time, engineOk and runInt and intScope.active)
[dOn, dO, dH, dL, dC, dHiBar, dLoBar, dHiT, dLoT, dInside, dBoth] = normStep(normDeep, open, high, low, close, bar_index, time, engineOk and runDeep and deepScope.active)

var bool resetInt = false
var bool resetDeep = false

int eMain = EVT_NONE
int eInt = EVT_NONE
int eDeep = EVT_NONE

if engineOk
    // MAIN always owns the chart-level structure.
    if mOn
        eMain := ctxStep(mainC, false, DIR_NONE, bar_index, mO, mH, mL, mC, mHiBar,
             mLoBar, mHiT, mLoT, histMain)
        zone(mainC, pbMainOn and showMain, 86, 68)
        markTaken(mainC, showMain, fadeMain + 20, histMain)

    // v0.7.6 OWNERSHIP RULE: Main correction START opens/replaces Internal scope.
    // Waiting for parent PB confirmation is too late: it discards the very bars
    // that form the nested Internal structure inside the pullback.
    if runInt and mainC.pbStarted
        openScope(intScope, mainC.det, bar_index, time)
        seedNorm(normInt, open, high, low, close, bar_index, time)
        resetInt := true
        // A new Internal owner invalidates the previous Deep owner.
        closeScope(deepScope)
        resetDeep := true

    // A Main CHoCH invalidates the previous directional PB scope until the next
    // published Main pullback establishes a fresh child owner.
    if eMain == EVT_CHOCH
        closeScope(intScope)
        closeScope(deepScope)
        resetInt := true
        resetDeep := true

    // INTERNAL only consumes raw candles while a Main PB owns its scope.
    if runInt and intScope.active and iOn
        eInt := ctxStep(intC, resetInt, DIR_NONE, bar_index, iO, iH, iL, iC, iHiBar,
             iLoBar, iHiT, iLoT, histInt)
        resetInt := false
        zone(intC, pbIntOn, 72, 74)
        markTaken(intC, true, fadeInt + 25, histInt)

    // Internal correction START opens/replaces Deep scope for the same reason.
    if runDeep and intScope.active and intC.pbStarted
        openScope(deepScope, intC.det, bar_index, time)
        seedNorm(normDeep, open, high, low, close, bar_index, time)
        resetDeep := true

    if eInt == EVT_CHOCH
        closeScope(deepScope)
        resetDeep := true

    // DEEP only consumes candles while an Internal PB owns its scope.
    if runDeep and deepScope.active and dOn
        eDeep := ctxStep(deepC, resetDeep, DIR_NONE, bar_index, dO, dH, dL, dC, dHiBar,
             dLoBar, dHiT, dLoT, histDeep)
        resetDeep := false
        zone(deepC, pbDeepOn, 82, 86)
        markTaken(deepC, true, fadeDeep + 25, histDeep)

    sweepDebug(mainC, showMain)

drawThreshold(mainC)
paint(mainC, showMain, "", 1, fadeMain, sizeOf(labelSizeMain))
paint(intC, runInt and intScope.active, "i", 1, fadeInt, sizeOf(labelSizeChild))
paint(deepC, runDeep and deepScope.active, "ii", 1, fadeDeep, sizeOf(labelSizeChild))

// [SRC] Strong / Weak are derived display semantics and feed nothing.
// Reference profile anchors the marker at the structural extreme itself,
// rather than placing the text at the far-right edge of the chart.
if showSW and showMain and barstate.islast and mainC.dir != DIR_NONE
    label.delete(mainC.weakDot)
    label.delete(mainC.weakTxt)
    label.delete(mainC.strongDot)
    label.delete(mainC.strongTxt)
    bool bull = mainC.dir == DIR_BULL
    if mainC.bos.on
        color wc = color.new(bull ? cBull : cBear, 10)
        mainC.weakDot := label.new(mainC.bos.barT, mainC.bos.px, "", xloc = xloc.bar_time,
             yloc = yloc.price, style = label.style_circle, color = color.new(wc, 25),
             textcolor = wc, size = size.tiny)
        mainC.weakTxt := label.new(mainC.bos.barT, mainC.bos.px + atr * 0.16,
             bull ? "HH | Weak High" : "LL | Weak Low", xloc = xloc.bar_time,
             yloc = yloc.price, style = label.style_none, color = na,
             textcolor = wc, size = size.tiny)
    if mainC.ch.on
        color sc = color.new(bull ? cBear : cBull, 10)
        mainC.strongDot := label.new(mainC.ch.barT, mainC.ch.px, "", xloc = xloc.bar_time,
             yloc = yloc.price, style = label.style_circle, color = color.new(sc, 25),
             textcolor = sc, size = size.tiny)
        mainC.strongTxt := label.new(mainC.ch.barT, mainC.ch.px - atr * 0.16,
             bull ? "HL | Strong Low" : "LH | Strong High", xloc = xloc.bar_time,
             yloc = yloc.price, style = label.style_none, color = na,
             textcolor = sc, size = size.tiny)

bool anyHS = mainC.bos.b.shadow or mainC.ch.b.shadow or mainC.idm.b.shadow or
     intC.bos.b.shadow or intC.ch.b.shadow
barcolor(anyHS ? cHS : showInside and mInside ? color.new(#b0bec5, 70) : na,
     title = "Structure tint")

// ═══════════════════════════ 9. PANELS ══════════════════════════════════════
dirTxt(int d) =>
    d == DIR_BULL ? "Bullish" : d == DIR_BEAR ? "Bearish" : "—"

phTxt(int p) =>
    p == PH_DISCOVER ? "seeking IDM" : p == PH_TRACK ? "IDM active" :
     p == PH_SEEK ? "BOS locked" : "boundary lock"

color cTxt = color.new(#787b86, 0)
color cVal = chart.fg_color

var table panel = table.new(position.top_right, 2, 5,
     bgcolor = color.new(chart.bg_color, 20), border_width = 1,
     border_color = color.new(#787b86, 60))
if showPanel and barstate.islast
    table.cell(panel, 0, 0, "Riptide LIT", text_color = cVal,
         text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(panel, 1, 0, mainOnly ? "MAIN ONLY" : "", text_color = cBear,
         text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(panel, 0, 1, "Main", text_color = cTxt, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(panel, 1, 1, dirTxt(mainC.dir) + " · " + phTxt(mainC.phase),
         text_size = size.small, text_color = mainC.dir == DIR_BULL ? cBull :
         mainC.dir == DIR_BEAR ? cBear : color.gray)
    table.cell(panel, 0, 2, "Internal", text_color = cTxt,
         text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(panel, 1, 2, runInt ? dirTxt(intC.dir) + " · " +
         phTxt(intC.phase) : "off", text_size = size.small,
         text_color = intC.dir == DIR_BULL ? cBull :
         intC.dir == DIR_BEAR ? cBear : color.gray)
    table.cell(panel, 0, 3, "Deep", text_color = cTxt, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(panel, 1, 3, runDeep ? dirTxt(deepC.dir) : "off",
         text_size = size.small, text_color = deepC.dir == DIR_BULL ? cBull :
         deepC.dir == DIR_BEAR ? cBear : color.gray)
    table.cell(panel, 0, 4, "BOS / CHoCH", text_color = cTxt,
         text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(panel, 1, 4,
         (mainC.bos.on ? str.tostring(mainC.bos.px, format.mintick) : "—") +
         "  /  " +
         (mainC.ch.on ? str.tostring(mainC.ch.px, format.mintick) : "—"),
         text_color = cVal, text_size = size.small)

// Developer invariant counters remain in each Ctx, but the old bottom-left
// debug table is deliberately removed from the reference profile. It obscured
// price and was not useful during normal calibration.

// Compact reference-shaped statistics table. The first two rows are now
// measured on the same first-passage population implied by the reference:
// an IDM is taken while BOTH BOS and CHoCH are active, then whichever boundary
// breaks first is counted. v0.7.9 also measures the source-described v1 near
// semantics (failed touch -> boundary break vs latest opposite pullback reach).
// These remain calibration statistics and never alter structural state.
pct(int n, int d) =>
    d > 0 ? str.tostring(100.0 * n / d, "#.0") + "%" : "—"

var table stat = table.new(position.bottom_right, 4, 7,
     bgcolor = color.new(chart.bg_color, 8), border_width = 1,
     border_color = color.new(#b0b3b8, 45))
if showStats and barstate.islast
    Ctx st = statsDepth == "Main" ? mainC : statsDepth == "Internal" ? intC : deepC
    color hdr = color.new(#d7e5f2, 0)
    color good = cBull
    color bad = cBear
    color muted = color.new(cTxt, 10)
    table.cell(stat, 0, 0, "Statistic", bgcolor = hdr, text_color = #263238, text_size = size.normal)
    table.cell(stat, 1, 0, "Total", bgcolor = hdr, text_color = #263238, text_size = size.normal)
    table.cell(stat, 2, 0, "Count", bgcolor = hdr, text_color = #263238, text_size = size.normal)
    table.cell(stat, 3, 0, "Rate", bgcolor = hdr, text_color = #263238, text_size = size.normal)

    table.cell(stat, 0, 1, "IDM → BOS touch", text_color = muted, text_size = size.normal)
    table.cell(stat, 1, 1, str.tostring(st.statIdmRaceTotal), text_color = cVal, text_size = size.normal)
    table.cell(stat, 2, 1, str.tostring(st.statIdmToBos), text_color = cVal, text_size = size.normal)
    table.cell(stat, 3, 1, pct(st.statIdmToBos, st.statIdmRaceTotal), text_color = good, text_size = size.normal)

    table.cell(stat, 0, 2, "IDM → Choch touch", text_color = muted, text_size = size.normal)
    table.cell(stat, 1, 2, str.tostring(st.statIdmRaceTotal), text_color = cVal, text_size = size.normal)
    table.cell(stat, 2, 2, str.tostring(st.statIdmToChoch), text_color = cVal, text_size = size.normal)
    table.cell(stat, 3, 2, pct(st.statIdmToChoch, st.statIdmRaceTotal), text_color = bad, text_size = size.normal)

    table.cell(stat, 0, 3, "BOS near → Opp PB reach", text_color = muted, text_size = size.normal)
    table.cell(stat, 1, 3, st.statBosNearTotal > 0 ? str.tostring(st.statBosNearTotal) : "—", text_color = cVal, text_size = size.normal)
    table.cell(stat, 2, 3, st.statBosNearTotal > 0 ? str.tostring(st.statBosNearOppPb) : "—", text_color = cVal, text_size = size.normal)
    table.cell(stat, 3, 3, st.statBosNearTotal > 0 ? pct(st.statBosNearOppPb, st.statBosNearTotal) : "—", text_color = good, text_size = size.normal)

    table.cell(stat, 0, 4, "BOS near → BOS break", text_color = muted, text_size = size.normal)
    table.cell(stat, 1, 4, st.statBosNearTotal > 0 ? str.tostring(st.statBosNearTotal) : "—", text_color = cVal, text_size = size.normal)
    table.cell(stat, 2, 4, st.statBosNearTotal > 0 ? str.tostring(st.statBosNearBreak) : "—", text_color = cVal, text_size = size.normal)
    table.cell(stat, 3, 4, st.statBosNearTotal > 0 ? pct(st.statBosNearBreak, st.statBosNearTotal) : "—", text_color = bad, text_size = size.normal)

    table.cell(stat, 0, 5, "Choch near → Opp PB reach", text_color = muted, text_size = size.normal)
    table.cell(stat, 1, 5, st.statChNearTotal > 0 ? str.tostring(st.statChNearTotal) : "—", text_color = cVal, text_size = size.normal)
    table.cell(stat, 2, 5, st.statChNearTotal > 0 ? str.tostring(st.statChNearOppPb) : "—", text_color = cVal, text_size = size.normal)
    table.cell(stat, 3, 5, st.statChNearTotal > 0 ? pct(st.statChNearOppPb, st.statChNearTotal) : "—", text_color = good, text_size = size.normal)

    table.cell(stat, 0, 6, "Choch near → Choch break", text_color = muted, text_size = size.normal)
    table.cell(stat, 1, 6, st.statChNearTotal > 0 ? str.tostring(st.statChNearTotal) : "—", text_color = cVal, text_size = size.normal)
    table.cell(stat, 2, 6, st.statChNearTotal > 0 ? str.tostring(st.statChNearBreak) : "—", text_color = cVal, text_size = size.normal)
    table.cell(stat, 3, 6, st.statChNearTotal > 0 ? pct(st.statChNearBreak, st.statChNearTotal) : "—", text_color = bad, text_size = size.normal)

// Temporary near-rule calibration table. This is deliberately separate from
// the reference-shaped result table so candidate research cannot be mistaken
// for a validated statistic. Targets from the supplied ZEC 30m reference are
// BOS near Total=29 and CHoCH near Total=14.
var table nearTbl = table.new(position.middle_right, 4, 9,
     bgcolor = color.new(chart.bg_color, 5), border_width = 1,
     border_color = color.new(#b0b3b8, 55))
if showNearScan and barstate.islast
    Ctx ns = statsDepth == "Main" ? mainC : statsDepth == "Internal" ? intC : deepC
    color nh = color.new(#eceff1, 0)
    table.cell(nearTbl, 0, 0, "Near candidate", bgcolor = nh, text_color = #263238, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(nearTbl, 1, 0, "BOS", bgcolor = nh, text_color = #263238, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(nearTbl, 2, 0, "Choch", bgcolor = nh, text_color = #263238, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(nearTbl, 3, 0, "Error", bgcolor = nh, text_color = #263238, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(nearTbl, 0, 1, "Reference target", text_color = cTxt, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(nearTbl, 1, 1, "29", text_color = cBull, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(nearTbl, 2, 1, "14", text_color = cBull, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(nearTbl, 3, 1, "0", text_color = cBull, text_size = size.small)
    int eTouch = math.abs(ns.calBosTouch - 29) + math.abs(ns.calChTouch - 14)
    int e10 = math.abs(ns.calBos10 - 29) + math.abs(ns.calCh10 - 14)
    int e20 = math.abs(ns.calBos20 - 29) + math.abs(ns.calCh20 - 14)
    int e25 = math.abs(ns.calBos25 - 29) + math.abs(ns.calCh25 - 14)
    int e33 = math.abs(ns.calBos33 - 29) + math.abs(ns.calCh33 - 14)
    int e50 = math.abs(ns.calBos50 - 29) + math.abs(ns.calCh50 - 14)
    int ePb = math.abs(ns.calBosPb - 29) + math.abs(ns.calChPb - 14)
    table.cell(nearTbl, 0, 2, "Raw level touch", text_color = cTxt, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(nearTbl, 1, 2, str.tostring(ns.calBosTouch), text_color = cVal, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(nearTbl, 2, 2, str.tostring(ns.calChTouch), text_color = cVal, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(nearTbl, 3, 2, str.tostring(eTouch), text_color = eTouch <= 4 ? cBull : cVal, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(nearTbl, 0, 3, "≤10% range", text_color = cTxt, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(nearTbl, 1, 3, str.tostring(ns.calBos10), text_color = cVal, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(nearTbl, 2, 3, str.tostring(ns.calCh10), text_color = cVal, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(nearTbl, 3, 3, str.tostring(e10), text_color = e10 <= 4 ? cBull : cVal, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(nearTbl, 0, 4, "≤20% range", text_color = cTxt, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(nearTbl, 1, 4, str.tostring(ns.calBos20), text_color = cVal, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(nearTbl, 2, 4, str.tostring(ns.calCh20), text_color = cVal, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(nearTbl, 3, 4, str.tostring(e20), text_color = e20 <= 4 ? cBull : cVal, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(nearTbl, 0, 5, "≤25% range", text_color = cTxt, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(nearTbl, 1, 5, str.tostring(ns.calBos25), text_color = cVal, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(nearTbl, 2, 5, str.tostring(ns.calCh25), text_color = cVal, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(nearTbl, 3, 5, str.tostring(e25), text_color = e25 <= 4 ? cBull : cVal, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(nearTbl, 0, 6, "≤33% range", text_color = cTxt, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(nearTbl, 1, 6, str.tostring(ns.calBos33), text_color = cVal, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(nearTbl, 2, 6, str.tostring(ns.calCh33), text_color = cVal, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(nearTbl, 3, 6, str.tostring(e33), text_color = e33 <= 4 ? cBull : cVal, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(nearTbl, 0, 7, "≤50% range", text_color = cTxt, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(nearTbl, 1, 7, str.tostring(ns.calBos50), text_color = cVal, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(nearTbl, 2, 7, str.tostring(ns.calCh50), text_color = cVal, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(nearTbl, 3, 7, str.tostring(e50), text_color = e50 <= 4 ? cBull : cVal, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(nearTbl, 0, 8, "≤1× last PB height", text_color = cTxt, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(nearTbl, 1, 8, str.tostring(ns.calBosPb), text_color = cVal, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(nearTbl, 2, 8, str.tostring(ns.calChPb), text_color = cVal, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(nearTbl, 3, 8, str.tostring(ePb), text_color = ePb <= 4 ? cBull : cVal, text_size = size.small)

// ═══════════════════════════ 10. ALERTS ═════════════════════════════════════
// Separate event types. None of them is a trade: this phase measures
// structure and makes no claim that any of it is tradeable.
bool aIdm = mainC.idm.on
bool aBos = mainC.bos.on
int aDir = mainC.dir
alertcondition(aIdm and not aIdm[1], "LIT IDM published",
     "Riptide LIT: inducement published")
alertcondition(not aIdm and aIdm[1], "LIT IDM taken",
     "Riptide LIT: inducement taken")
alertcondition(aBos and not aBos[1], "LIT BOS locked",
     "Riptide LIT: BOS locked")
alertcondition(not aBos and aBos[1], "LIT BOS broken",
     "Riptide LIT: BOS broken - continuation")
alertcondition(aDir != aDir[1] and aDir != 0, "LIT trend flip",
     "Riptide LIT: CHoCH broken - trend flipped")
